# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fonto environment variables
#
# Legend (R = required, O = optional):
#   [R]  required at runtime — feature breaks/throws without it
#   [O]  optional — feature gracefully disabled if unset
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── App identity ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [R] Public app origin — used for OAuth callbacks, cookies, presigned-URL hosts.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3500
# [O] Postgres schema namespace for Fonto's tables. Defaults to "public".
APP_SCHEMA_NAMESPACE=fonto

# ── Database (Fonto's own tables) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# [R] Postgres URL for Drizzle. Without it: every DB query throws on first use.
#     Phase 4.3 (ADR 0002): requires the `pgvector` extension installed in
#     the database. Migration 0017 enables it via
#     `CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector`. Probe at runtime with
#     `GET /api/health?check=vector` (returns 503 if missing).
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:password@127.0.0.1:5432/fonto

# ── Better Auth (identity) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [R] Postgres URL for the shared `auth` schema (user, session, account tables).
#     Falls back to DATABASE_URL if unset.
AUTH_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:password@127.0.0.1:5432/fonto
# [R] Session-signing secret. Generate: `openssl rand -hex 32`
#     If sharing identity with other Joeybuilt apps, this MUST match theirs.
AUTH_SECRET=generate_with_openssl_rand_hex_32
# [O] Better Auth canonical base URL. Defaults to NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL.
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3500

# ── Personal Access Tokens (Phase 2.1) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Programmatic API auth lives in the `fonto.api_keys` table; users mint tokens
# from /app/settings/tokens. No env knobs are required — prefix (`fonto_pat_`),
# headers (`Authorization: Bearer`, `x-api-key`), scopes (read/write/admin),
# and the per-key rate limit (600 req / 60 s) are constants in
# `lib/auth/api-keys.ts`. To tighten or loosen the rate limit edit the
# `API_KEY_RATE_LIMIT` const there. Distributed rate limiting belongs at the
# edge (Caddy / Cloudflare), not here.

# ── Published API surface (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] Inbound service key for Fonto's published API (`/api/peer/v1/*`). A peer
#     or agent that wants Fonto's data authenticates with this key. Unset ⇒ the
#     peer surface answers 503 FEATURE_DISABLED, and that is a supported state —
#     no core flow depends on it.
# FONTO_SERVICE_KEY=
# [O] Optional second inbound key, accepted in parallel (rotation without a
#     coordinated deploy).
# FONTO_SERVICE_KEY_V2=
# [O] Pins intelligence resolution to the embedded tier: "1"/"true" disables the
#     optional remote (federated) tier entirely. Unset ⇒ the embedded tier is
#     still the terminal floor.
# JEX_FEDERATION_OFF=

# ── OCR (Phase 4.4) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OCR runs through the vision sidecar (FONTO_VISION_URL, PaddleOCR PP-OCRv5).
# Without it, OCR is skipped; errors are recorded as `failed` and the asset is
# left for the nightly backfill cron to retry.
#
# [O] Default language hint passed to PaddleOCR. PP-OCRv5 supports 80+
#     languages out of the box; pass an ISO-639-1 code (e.g. `en`, `zh`,
#     `ja`, `de`). Default: `en`.
# OCR_DEFAULT_LANG=en
#
# [O] Default batch size for the nightly OCR backfill cron. PaddleOCR is
#     fast enough that 50 is a comfortable floor — bump to several hundred
#     on a fast vision sidecar. Clamped to 1..500 per call. Default: 50.
# OCR_BACKFILL_BATCH_SIZE=50

# ── Vision tier (Phase 4.2 — CLIP image embeddings) ──────────────────────────
# [O] Base URL of the vision sidecar. The fonto worker posts to
#     {FONTO_VISION_URL}/vision/clip/{image,text} to embed assets + queries.
#     Without it: CLIP search returns `{ results: [], unavailable: true }` and
#     the embed worker no-ops — a supported state.
# FONTO_VISION_URL=
# [O] Optional bearer key sent to the vision sidecar (self-hosted sidecars on
#     a private network usually need none).
# FONTO_VISION_KEY=
# [O] Worker container only. Concurrency for the CLIP embedding worker.
#     Network-bound but the vision service is itself CPU-bound, so keep this
#     modest to avoid hammering it.
# CLIP_EMBED_CONCURRENCY=4
# [O] Phase 5.1 — face detection + ArcFace embedding worker concurrency.
#     The fonto worker posts to `{FONTO_VISION_URL}/v1/faces/detect`; the
#     sidecar runs RetinaFace + ArcFace and returns one face block per
#     detection. Network-bound but the vision service is GPU/CPU-bound, so
#     keep this conservative (default 2). Without FONTO_VISION_URL the
#     face-detect worker no-ops + logs a warning.
# FACE_DETECT_CONCURRENCY=2
# [O] Phase 5.4 — TTL for the in-memory CLIP text-embedding cache that
#     backs the smart-collection `clipText` predicate. Default 3600000 ms
#     (1 h). Saved queries change rarely, so the embedding is effectively
#     stable; caching cuts vision-sidecar load on smart-collection refresh
#     to near zero. Eviction on TTL expiry or LRU overflow.
# CLIP_TEXT_CACHE_TTL_MS=3600000
# [O] Phase 5.4 — max entries in the in-memory CLIP text-embedding cache
#     above. Default 100. Each entry is ~4 KB (512 floats), so the cap is
#     ~400 KB of memory per process. Bump only if you have many distinct
#     `clipText` smart collections refreshing concurrently.
# CLIP_TEXT_CACHE_MAX=100
# [O] Bulk-import escape hatch. When 1, createAssetRow skips the inline
#     CLIP-similarity dedup embed so import throughput isn't bounded by the
#     vision sidecar. Skipped assets are covered by the clip-embedding
#     backfill queue afterwards. Set only for one-shot import scripts.
# FONTO_IMPORT_SKIP_INLINE_CLIP=1

# ── Auto-classification (Phase 4.6) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] Minimum CLIP cosine for a zero-shot classification to be trusted.
#     Below this we defer to the LLM classifier (slower + costs tokens, but
#     better when CLIP is uncertain). Default 0.18 — CLIP image+text
#     cosines rarely exceed 0.3 even on strong matches.
# CLASSIFY_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD=0.18
# [O] Where to persist the embedded taxonomy vector cache. Defaults to
#     ~/.fonto/classify-vectors.json. Safe to delete to force a re-embed
#     (e.g. after editing `lib/classify/taxonomy.ts`). Cache is
#     auto-invalidated on embedding-model change.
# CLASSIFY_VECTOR_CACHE_PATH=/var/lib/fonto/classify-vectors.json

# ── Cloudflare R2 / S3-compatible storage (required for uploads) ─────────────
# [R] R2 bucket name where assets are stored.
R2_BUCKET=fonto-assets
# [R] R2 access key ID.
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your_r2_access_key_id
# [R] R2 secret access key.
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your_r2_secret_access_key
# [R] R2 endpoint URL. For Cloudflare R2:
#     https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
R2_ENDPOINT=https://your-account-id.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# [O] Public CDN domain for asset URLs. Without it: presigned URLs are used.
# R2_PUBLIC_URL=https://assets.yourdomain.com

# ── Direct-to-R2 uploads (Phase 1.2) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] Hard cap on POST /api/v1/assets/init size declarations, in bytes.
#     Default: 524288000 (500 MB). The legacy multipart POST keeps its own
#     50 MB cap (memory-bounded) regardless of this value.
# MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=524288000
# [O] If "true", POST /api/v1/assets/:id/complete trusts a client-supplied
#     SHA-256 (if present) and skips the server-side stream-hash pass. Use
#     only when clients you control compute checksums correctly.
# SKIP_SERVER_CHECKSUM=false
# [O] Client-side feature flag — when "true", the web UI uses uploadDirect()
#     (presigned PUT) instead of the legacy multipart POST. Default: false.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DIRECT_UPLOAD=false

# ── Transactional email (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] Resend API key for password-reset / verification emails. Without it:
#     those flows error at the moment they're invoked.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...

# ── Cron security (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] Shared secret required by /api/cron/* endpoints. Without it: cron routes
#     return 401. Generate: `openssl rand -hex 32`
# CRON_SECRET=generate_with_openssl_rand_hex_32

# ── Background jobs (BullMQ + Redis/Valkey) ──────────────────────────────────
# [O] Redis/Valkey connection URL. Defaults to redis://valkey:6379 (matches
#     the platform's Valkey service). Both the Next.js app (producer) and the
#     fonto-worker container (consumer) must point at the same instance.
# REDIS_URL=redis://valkey:6379
# [O] Worker container only. Number of concurrent jobs per worker process.
# WORKER_CONCURRENCY=4
# [O] Worker container only. Concurrency for the Phase 1.1 thumbnails worker.
#     Lower than WORKER_CONCURRENCY by default because sharp encodes are
#     CPU-bound and contend with the umbrella processAsset worker for cores.
# THUMBNAIL_WORKER_CONCURRENCY=2
# [O] Pino log level for both the app and the worker. info | debug | warn | error
# LOG_LEVEL=info
# [O] Reaper threshold: a row stuck in processing_state='processing' longer
#     than this many minutes is considered abandoned by a dead worker and is
#     either re-enqueued (if processing_attempts < 5) or terminally failed.
#     Defaults to 60.
# REAPER_STUCK_THRESHOLD_MINUTES=60
# [O] Reaper tick interval (ms). How often the maintenance worker re-runs the
#     stuck-assets sweep. Defaults to 300000 (5 minutes).
# REAPER_INTERVAL_MS=300000

# ── Image decoding (HEIC + camera RAW) ───────────────────────────────────────
# [O] Hard timeout (ms) per RAW/HEIC decode subprocess (dcraw_emu,
#     heif-convert). Pathological files are killed and the thumbnail is
#     recorded as failed rather than blocking the worker. Defaults to 30000.
# RAW_DECODE_TIMEOUT_MS=30000

# ── Bull-board sidecar (queue admin UI) ──────────────────────────────────────
# The bull-board sidecar (Dockerfile.bullboard) exposes the BullMQ admin UI
# behind HTTP Basic Auth. The Next.js app links to it from /admin/jobs when
# BULL_BOARD_URL is set; otherwise the page renders the live-counts fallback.
# [O] Public URL where bull-board is reachable. Set this in the Next.js app
#     env so /admin/jobs surfaces a link. Should be the externally-routable
#     URL (e.g. https://ops.example.com/fonto/jobs/), NOT the internal
#     container DNS name.
# BULL_BOARD_URL=https://ops.example.com/fonto/jobs/
# [R for sidecar] Basic-auth username. Sidecar refuses to start if unset.
# BULL_BOARD_BASIC_AUTH_USER=ops
# [R for sidecar] Basic-auth password. Sidecar refuses to start if unset.
#     Generate: `openssl rand -hex 24`
# BULL_BOARD_BASIC_AUTH_PASS=generate_with_openssl_rand_hex_24
# [O] Port the bull-board Express app listens on. Defaults to 3300.
# BULL_BOARD_PORT=3300

# ── Observability: Prometheus + OpenTelemetry (Phase 0.5) ────────────────────
# [O] Static bearer token required to scrape `/api/metrics` (web) and the
#     worker's `/metrics` endpoint. If UNSET, both endpoints return 503 —
#     metrics are never served anonymously. Generate: `openssl rand -hex 32`
# METRICS_BEARER_TOKEN=generate_with_openssl_rand_hex_32
#
# [O] Worker container only. Port for the bare-Node metrics HTTP listener.
#     Defaults to 9464 (the OTel community default for Prom HTTP exposers).
# WORKER_METRICS_PORT=9464
#
# [O] OTLP/HTTP base endpoint for traces + metrics (e.g. the Joeybuilt OTel
#     collector). If unset, the OTel SDK is NOT started — Fonto runs fine
#     without a collector.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://otel-collector:4318
#
# [O] Override the OTel service name. Defaults: `fonto-web` for the app,
#     `fonto-worker` for the worker.
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=fonto-web

# ── Resumable uploads via tus (Phase 1.4) ────────────────────────────────────
# The /api/v1/uploads/tus endpoint accepts chunked resumable uploads for large
# files (4K videos, RAWs, multi-gigabyte archives). Chunks stream directly to
# R2 multipart; on completion the assembled object is moved to the canonical
# asset key and a `fonto.assets` row is inserted.
#
# [O] Maximum upload size in bytes. Default 10737418240 (10 GiB). Increase if
#     you ingest very large video originals; R2 itself caps objects at 5 TiB.
# TUS_MAX_FILE_SIZE_BYTES=10737418240
#
# [O] Multipart part size in bytes. Default 8388608 (8 MiB). Must be >= 5 MiB
#     (S3 minimum) and ideally divides cleanly into your typical file size.
# TUS_PART_SIZE_BYTES=8388608

# ── Outbound webhooks (Phase 2.4) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fonto can POST signed JSON payloads to user-registered endpoints when assets,
# tags, or collections change. The worker container drains the delivery queue
# and re-enqueues with exponential backoff (1m, 5m, 15m, 1h, 6h) on failure;
# attempts cap at 6.
#
# [O] Number of concurrent webhook POSTs per worker process. Network-bound,
#     so this can be higher than CPU-bound workers without contention.
#     Defaults to 4.
# WEBHOOK_DELIVERY_CONCURRENCY=4
#
# [O] Per-request HTTP timeout in milliseconds. Defaults to 10000 (10s).
#     A slow subscriber that exceeds this is treated as a failed delivery
#     and retried per the backoff schedule.
# WEBHOOK_TIMEOUT_MS=10000

# ── Workspace invitations (Phase 3.3) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Multi-user workspaces use email-keyed invitations that produce
# `workspace_memberships` rows on acceptance. The invitation token is a random
# 32-byte URL-safe value stored in plaintext — the short TTL bounds the risk
# and the settings UI re-shows the URL when the recipient loses the original
# email. See ADR 0004 for the model.
#
# Email delivery is intentionally stubbed in Phase 3.3 (Phase 7.3 lands real
# email infrastructure). Until then the invitation API returns the token + URL
# in the response so the inviter can paste it into their preferred channel.
#
# [O] Invitation lifetime in days. Default 7; clamped to 1–365. Existing
#     invitations keep their original expiry — this only affects new ones.
# WORKSPACE_INVITATION_TTL_DAYS=7

# ── Share links (Phase 2.5) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public share links can be password-protected (argon2id), view-capped, and
# expire at a configurable time. Access events are persisted to
# fonto.share_link_views for analytics + abuse forensics — but the raw client
# IP is NEVER stored. We hash it as sha256(SHARE_LINK_IP_SALT + ip), so the
# salt MUST be set to a non-trivial random value in production. Rotating the
# salt invalidates all existing ipHash analytics (deliberate).
#
# [R for /share/*] Per-deploy random salt for share-link IP hashing.
#     Generate: `openssl rand -hex 32`. If unset in prod, /share routes still
#     work but the privacy guarantee weakens to a known-constant fallback.
# SHARE_LINK_IP_SALT=generate_with_openssl_rand_hex_32

# ── Audit log (Phase 3.2) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every mutating action (asset upload/update/delete, share create/revoke,
# token mint/revoke, webhook CRUD, etc.) is recorded to `fonto.audit_log`
# with the actor, target, truncated IP subnet (/24 IPv4, /48 IPv6 — NEVER
# the raw client IP), and User-Agent (capped at 500 chars). A daily BullMQ
# maintenance job prunes rows older than the retention window.
#
# Workspace owners can view their workspace's audit log at
# `/app/settings/audit` (gated on `requireWorkspaceOwner`).
#
# [O] How many days to keep audit_log rows before the reaper deletes them.
#     Default 90. Set lower for stricter privacy, higher for longer
#     compliance windows.
# AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS=90
#
# [O] Reaper tick interval in milliseconds. Default 86400000 (24h).
#     Lowering this only changes how often the prune runs — it does not
#     change which rows are eligible (always older than AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS).
# AUDIT_PRUNE_INTERVAL_MS=86400000

# ── Duplicate detection (Phase 4.5) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Fonto runs two passes of duplicate detection on every image upload:
#
#   1. pHash (always on; sub-millisecond): 64-bit perceptual hash with a
#      Hamming-distance ≤ 5 threshold. Catches identical images, different
#      resizes / JPEG qualities, and minor color shifts.
#
#   2. CLIP cosine similarity (Phase 4.5; requires a vision service): runs
#      ONLY when pHash didn't find a match. Catches re-crops, color-graded
#      re-edits, and different framings of the same scene that share semantic
#      content. The default threshold matches Immich's pre-tuned value.
#
# The CLIP pass runs inline in the upload request when it finishes within
# CLIP_DEDUP_INLINE_TIMEOUT_MS; otherwise the check is deferred to the
# `clip-dedup-check` BullMQ worker so the upload response isn't blocked.
#
# Both knobs degrade safely: with no vision service wired (FONTO_VISION_URL
# unset) the CLIP pass is a no-op and pHash continues to work.
#
# [O] CLIP cosine similarity threshold (0..1, higher = stricter). Matches
#     above this are flagged. Default 0.92. Tune higher to reduce false
#     positives, lower to catch more borderline scenes.
# CLIP_DEDUP_THRESHOLD=0.92
#
# [O] Inline embed budget in milliseconds. If the vision call exceeds this,
#     the dedup check is deferred to the worker (the upload still completes
#     immediately, just without the inline banner). Default 2000.
# CLIP_DEDUP_INLINE_TIMEOUT_MS=2000
#
# [O] Worker concurrency for the clip-dedup-check queue. Default 2.
# CLIP_DEDUP_WORKER_CONCURRENCY=2
#
# [O] Delay (ms) before re-enqueueing a clip-dedup job when the upstream
#     CLIP embedding hasn't been written to the row yet. Default 30000.
# CLIP_DEDUP_RETRY_DELAY_MS=30000

# ── Memories / "On this day" (Phase 5.3) ─────────────────────────────────────
# `GET /api/v1/memories` returns assets captured on the same MM-DD in prior
# years. Both knobs are read at request time; no restart needed for changes.
#
# [O] Day-of-year fuzz window. ±N days around the requested date are
#     considered the "same day". Default 3 — May 23 also pulls in May 20..26.
#     Set 0 for an exact-day match. Larger values surface more content per
#     query but inflate the per-year bucket count.
# MEMORIES_DAY_WINDOW=3
#
# [O] Hard cap on assets returned per year, applied *after* the SQL
#     LIMIT 200. Stops a single high-volume year (e.g. wedding day) from
#     dominating the carousel. Default 50.
# MEMORIES_MAX_PER_YEAR=50

# ── Stacks (Phase 5.5) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Manual stacks group related assets where one is "primary" — RAW+JPEG of the
# same shot, an iPhone burst, multiple edits of the same photo. The auto-
# suggester (`GET /api/v1/stacks/suggestions`) is read-only — it flags
# candidate clusters and the user confirms each via
# `POST /api/v1/stacks/suggestions/accept`. Stacks are never created
# automatically.
#
# [O] Burst window in seconds. 3+ assets within this window from the same
#     camera become a burst-stack suggestion. Default 5. Pairs are
#     intentionally skipped — they're more likely an intentional double than
#     a burst.
# STACK_BURST_THRESHOLD_S=5
#
# [O] RAW+JPEG window in seconds. Two assets within this window from the
#     same camera, one image/jpeg and one canonical RAW (CR2/CR3/DNG/ARW
#     /NEF/etc — see lib/mime.ts:RAW_MIME_TYPES), become a raw+jpeg-stack
#     suggestion. Default 2.
# STACK_RAW_JPEG_THRESHOLD_S=2

# ── Payments (Joeybuilt Cloud only — NOT implemented yet) ────────────────────
# Stripe billing is reserved for a future Joeybuilt Cloud tier. Self-hosted
# instances should leave STRIPE_SECRET_KEY unset — it has no effect today.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Compose / self-hosting
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# These are consumed by docker-compose.yml. See docs/self-hosting.md.
#
# [R] Postgres password (compose). `openssl rand -hex 24`
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# [O] Postgres user / database name. Defaults: fonto / fonto.
# POSTGRES_USER=fonto
# POSTGRES_DB=fonto
# [R] Redis/Valkey password (compose). `openssl rand -hex 24`
# REDIS_PASSWORD=
# [R] SHARE_LINK_IP_SALT — see the Security section above.
# [O] Compose MinIO credentials — see the R2 section above for the
#     endpoint-reachability caveat that decides whether uploads work.
# MINIO_ROOT_USER=fonto
# MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=
# [O] Bind/port for the web container. Defaults: 127.0.0.1 / 3500. Change the
#     bind to 0.0.0.0 only if this host is intentionally public.
# FONTOWEB_BIND=127.0.0.1
# FONTOWEB_PORT=3500
# [O] Node heap ceiling for `next build` (MB). Default 4096; below ~4096 the
#     build dies with exit 134. CI uses 6144.
# NODE_HEAP_MB=4096
# [O] Public domain for the `selfhosted` (Caddy) profile. Required for that profile.
# PUBLIC_DOMAIN=
# [O] Grafana admin login (observability profile). Password is required there.
# GRAFANA_ADMIN_USER=admin
# GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# [O] Host dir holding alertmanager secret files (observability profile).
# ALERTMANAGER_SECRETS_DIR=./ops/secrets
# [O] PGPASSWORD for the `backup` profile's postgres-backup sidecar.
# PGPASSWORD=
# [O] Backup sidecar cadence/retention. Defaults: 86400 s / 7 days.
# BACKUP_INTERVAL_SECONDS=86400
# BACKUP_RETENTION_DAYS=7

# ── Signup / instance administration ─────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] "true" allows open self-registration. Default (unset/false): invite-only,
#     except the FIRST user on a fresh instance, who is always allowed so you
#     can bootstrap.
# FONTO_ALLOW_OPEN_SIGNUP=false
# [O] Comma-separated emails auto-granted instance-admin. Default "".
# FONTO_INSTANCE_ADMINS=

# ── Passkeys / WebAuthn ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] WebAuthn rpId. Derived from the app origin when unset (must be a registrable
#     suffix of that origin, e.g. example.com for https://app.example.com).
#     Baked into every registered credential — changing it later forces ALL
#     users to re-register. Set it deliberately before your first user.
# PASSKEY_RP_ID=
# [O] WebAuthn origin. Derived as https://<RP_ID> when unset.
# PASSKEY_ORIGIN=
# [O] Human-readable name shown in the OS passkey prompt. Default "Fonto".
# PASSKEY_RP_NAME=Fonto

# ── OIDC / SSO (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The provider is dormant unless CLIENT_ID, CLIENT_SECRET and DISCOVERY_URL are set.
# [O] Discovery document URL of your IdP (Authentik, Keycloak, ...).
# OIDC_DISCOVERY_URL=
# [O] Provider id used in callback paths. Default "sso".
# OIDC_PROVIDER_ID=sso
# [O] Space-separated scopes. Default "openid profile email".
# OIDC_SCOPES=openid profile email
# [O] Base URL for OAuth redirects. Falls back to BETTER_AUTH_URL.
# OIDC_REDIRECT_BASE_URL=
# [O] Build-time twin of OIDC_PROVIDER_ID, inlined into the client bundle.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_OIDC_PROVIDER_ID=

# ── Additional trusted origins (optional) ────────────────────────────────────
# [O] Comma-separated extra origins accepted for auth callbacks (e.g. a mobile
#     app scheme or a second hostname). Default "".
# EXTRA_TRUSTED_ORIGINS=

# ── Google OAuth (optional integration) ──────────────────────────────────────
# [O] Enables Google sign-in and calendar/contacts import. Unset ⇒ integration hidden.
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── AI: app-owned connections ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Users configure their OWN connection in Settings → Integrations (label, base
# URL, model, API key; key encrypted at rest). These env vars supply the
# DEPLOYMENT DEFAULT used when a user has none — e.g. a shared LiteLLM gateway.
# Unset ⇒ no deployment default; AI features degrade per capability.
# [O] OpenAI-compatible base URL, e.g. http://my-gateway:4000/v1
# AI_BASE_URL=
# [O] Bearer key for that endpoint.
# AI_API_KEY=
# [O] Model id the connection is called with (a gateway may use "auto").
# AI_MODEL=auto
# [O] Label shown for the deployment default in the settings UI.
# AI_LABEL=LiteLLM Auto
# Legacy names, still honored (read order: AI_* first):
# FONTO_LLM_BASE_URL=
# FONTO_LLM_KEY=

# ── Email (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] From-address for invitations/digests. Default derived from the app origin.
# EMAIL_FROM=
# [O] Public base URL used in digest links. Default http://localhost:3500.
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3500

# ── Push notifications (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] Firebase service-account JSON (or its path) for mobile push. Unset ⇒ push disabled.
# FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=

# ── Android app-links (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] SHA-256 fingerprint served at /.well-known/assetlinks.json. Unset ⇒ the
#     endpoint returns 503 and app links do not verify.
# ASSETLINKS_SHA256=

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Tuning knobs
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Everything below is OPTIONAL with a working default. Listed so you can find
# them; leave commented unless you have a reason. Values shown are the defaults.

# ── Database pool / pooling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] Max pg pool connections. Default 20.
# FONTO_PG_POOL_MAX=20
# [O] "true" forces path-style S3 addressing. Inferred from the endpoint host
#     when unset (required for MinIO, off for R2).
# S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=

# ── Uploads / imports ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] Ceiling for the LEGACY multipart upload path. Default 52428800 (50 MB).
# LEGACY_MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=52428800
# [O] Ceiling for an uploaded import ZIP. Default 5368709120 (5 GiB).
# MAX_IMPORT_ZIP_BYTES=5368709120
# [O] Size ceiling for streamed thumbnail extraction. Default 5368709120 (5 GiB).
# THUMBNAIL_MAX_STREAMED_BYTES=5368709120

# ── Local filesystem mirror (optional second storage backend) ────────────────
# [O] Root dir for the local-fs mirror. Unset ⇒ local-fs paths are skipped
#     (R2/S3 only). In compose this is /data/fonto-media inside the
#     `local-storage` volume.
# LOCAL_STORAGE_ROOT=/data/fonto-media

# ── S3 one-off import (scripts/import-from-s3.ts) ────────────────────────────
# [O] Source bucket credentials for the bulk importer. Default region us-east-1.
# S3_IMPORT_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# S3_IMPORT_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# S3_IMPORT_REGION=us-east-1

# ── Worker concurrency / timing ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] BullMQ lock duration (ms). Default 300000.
# WORKER_LOCK_DURATION_MS=300000
# [O] Stalled-job check interval (ms). Default 60000.
# WORKER_STALLED_INTERVAL_MS=60000
# [O] HLS transcode concurrency. Default 1.
# VIDEO_HLS_CONCURRENCY=1
# [O] Import-job concurrency. Default 1.
# IMPORT_WORKER_CONCURRENCY=1
# [O] Evidence-extraction concurrency. Default 3.
# EVIDENCE_EXTRACT_CONCURRENCY=3
# [O] Date-inference concurrency. Default 4.
# INFER_DATE_CONCURRENCY=4
# [O] Storage sync worker concurrency. Default 3.
# STORAGE_SYNC_WORKER_CONCURRENCY=3
# [O] Clip-embedding preview retry budget. Defaults: 30000 ms / 20.
# CLIP_EMBED_PREVIEW_DELAY_MS=30000
# CLIP_EMBED_PREVIEW_MAX_RETRIES=20
# [O] Clip-dedup retry cap. Default 40.
# CLIP_DEDUP_MAX_RETRIES=40

# ── HLS / video encoding ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] Each is "0"-to-disable (they default ON). fMP4 segments, stream-copy
#     fast path, and HDR→SDR tonemapping. Defaults: enabled.
# FONTO_HLS_FMP4=1
# FONTO_HLS_COPY_FASTPATH=1
# FONTO_HLS_HDR_TONEMAP=1
# [O] Bitrate ceiling (bps) for the copy fast path. Default 12000000.
# FONTO_HLS_COPY_MAX_BITRATE=12000000

# ── Reaper (stuck/stranded asset recovery) ───────────────────────────────────
# [O] Batch sizes for the reaper passes. Defaults: 200 each.
# REAPER_STUCK_BATCH=200
# REAPER_SYNC_STRANDED_BATCH=200
# REAPER_THUMBNAIL_BACKFILL_BATCH=200
# [O] Minutes before a sync is considered stranded. Default 60.
# REAPER_SYNC_STRANDED_THRESHOLD_MINUTES=60

# ── Storage reconcile / backfill ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] Enable the passes (non-empty/"true" to opt in; default off).
# STORAGE_BACKFILL=
# STORAGE_RECONCILE=
# [O] Batch sizes. Defaults: 200 (backfill), 1000 (reconcile).
# STORAGE_BACKFILL_BATCH_SIZE=200
# STORAGE_RECONCILE_BATCH_SIZE=1000
# [O] Intervals (ms). Defaults: 300000 (backfill), 86400000 (reconcile).
# STORAGE_BACKFILL_INTERVAL_MS=300000
# STORAGE_RECONCILE_INTERVAL_MS=86400000
# [O] Legacy alias for the reconcile interval (ms). Default 86400000.
# RECONCILE_STORAGE_INTERVAL_MS=86400000

# ── Scheduled backfills (worker) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] Enable flags; default off (set to "true" to opt in).
# BACKFILL_EVIDENCE=
# BACKFILL_FACE_CROPS=
# BACKFILL_INFERENCE=
# BACKFILL_VARIANT_CANDIDATES=
# [O] Batch sizes. Defaults: 100 (evidence), 200 (inference).
# BACKFILL_EVIDENCE_BATCH_SIZE=100
# BACKFILL_INFERENCE_BATCH_SIZE=200
# [O] Batch size for the face-crop backfill. Default 25 (DEFAULT_BACKFILL_BATCH_SIZE).
# BACKFILL_FACE_CROPS_BATCH_SIZE=25
# [O] Intervals (ms). Defaults: 300000 for the 5-minute passes,
#     86400000 for variant candidates.
# BACKFILL_EVIDENCE_INTERVAL_MS=300000
# BACKFILL_FACE_CROPS_INTERVAL_MS=300000
# BACKFILL_INFERENCE_INTERVAL_MS=300000
# BACKFILL_VARIANT_CANDIDATES_INTERVAL_MS=86400000

# ── Face clustering / matching ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] "1" disables the nightly face-cluster sweep entirely.
# FACE_CLUSTER_DISABLED=
# [O] "1" disables only the GPU edge-builder path (falls back to CPU).
# FACE_CLUSTER_GPU_DISABLED=
# [O] Max faces per cluster run. Default 50000.
# FACE_CLUSTER_MAX_N=50000
# [O] Minimum detection confidence to include a face. Default 0.55.
# FACE_CLUSTER_MIN_CONFIDENCE=0.55
# [O] Cosine-distance epsilon for auto-matching. Default 0.26 (CPU/GPU parity).
# FACE_MATCH_EPS_AUTO=0.26
# [O] Nightly cluster cadence (ms). Default 86400000.
# AUTO_CLUSTER_INTERVAL_MS=86400000

# ── Auto-stacking ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] Enable the auto-stack suggester. Default true.
# AUTO_STACK_ENABLED=true
# [O] Cadence (ms). Default 86400000.
# AUTO_STACK_INTERVAL_MS=86400000
# [O] Max members per auto-stack. Default 30.
# STACK_AUTO_MAX_MEMBERS=30
# [O] Near-duplicate pHash Hamming distance. Default 4.
# STACK_NEARDUP_HAMMING=4
# [O] Near-duplicate time window (s). Default 60.
# STACK_NEARDUP_WINDOW_S=60
# [O] Screenshot-run threshold (s). Default 30.
# STACK_SCREENSHOT_RUN_THRESHOLD_S=30

# ── Variant candidates (near-duplicate evidence) ─────────────────────────────
# [O] CLIP similarity threshold. Default 0.97.
# VARIANT_CLIP_THRESHOLD=0.97
# [O] pHash Hamming threshold. Default 5.
# VARIANT_PHASH_THRESHOLD=5
# [O] Max assets per variant group. Default 12.
# VARIANT_MAX_GROUP_SIZE=12

# ── Classification thresholds ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] Softmax floor for accepting a label. Default 0.15.
# CLASSIFY_ARGMAX_FLOOR=0.15
# [O] Minimum gap to the runner-up before a label is trusted. Default 0.05.
# CLASSIFY_RUNNER_UP_DELTA=0.05

# ── Re-audit drift sweep ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] Max assets re-audited per run. Default 5000.
# DRIFT_SWEEP_MAX_PER_RUN=5000
# [O] Age (days) at which an audit is considered stale. Default 7.
# DRIFT_SWEEP_STALE_DAYS=7

# ── Places / events ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] Minimum assets before a place is surfaced. Default 3.
# PLACES_MIN_ASSETS=3
# [O] Gap (hours) that splits an event. Default 3. NEXT_PUBLIC_* ⇒ inlined at build.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_EVENT_GAP_HOURS=3

# ── Feature flags ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [O] Split library surfaces (photos/documents tabs). Default off.
# LIBRARY_SURFACE_SPLIT_ENABLED=
# [O] Prefixes treated as "shoot" dirs during import scoping. Default "".
# FONTO_SHOOT_DIR_PREFIXES=
# [O] Daily digest cadence (ms). Default 86400000.
# DIGEST_INTERVAL_MS=86400000

# ── Worker autoscaler (ops/autoscaler, compose `autoscaler` profile) ────────
# [O] "1" logs decisions without touching compose. Default in compose: 1.
# AUTOSCALER_DRY_RUN=1
# [O] Compose file the autoscaler inspects. Default /etc/fonto-compose/docker-compose.yml.
# AUTOSCALER_COMPOSE_FILE=/etc/fonto-compose/docker-compose.yml
# [O] Service it scales. Default fonto-worker.
# AUTOSCALER_WORKER_SERVICE=fonto-worker
# [O] Env file it passes through on scale. Default unset.
# AUTOSCALER_ENV_FILE=
# [O] Comma-separated queues it watches.
#     Default asset-processing,thumbnails,clip-embedding,face-detect,ocr.
# AUTOSCALER_QUEUES=asset-processing,thumbnails,clip-embedding,face-detect,ocr

# ── Test / e2e only (never needed in production) ─────────────────────────────
# [O] Playwright base URL and login for the e2e suites.
# PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3500
# PLAYWRIGHT_EMAIL=
# PLAYWRIGHT_PASSWORD=
# [O] Set to 1 to run e2e against a Chromium already installed on the host.
# PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM=
# [O] Playwright's own base URL (default http://127.0.0.1:3500). Distinct from
#     PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL, which the e2e scripts use for a live instance.
# BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3500
# [O] Output dir for e2e/passkey-shots.mjs screenshots. Default /tmp/shots.
# OUT=/tmp/shots

# ── CLI (cli/ — see cli/README.md) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The CLI stores its config in ~/.config/fonto-cli-nodejs/config.json and has
# NO default base URL on purpose: a baked production hostname in a public repo
# would point every third-party install at an instance they do not own.
# `fonto login --base-url <url>` writes it; these override per-invocation.
# [R] Your instance origin, e.g. http://localhost:3500
# FONTO_BASE_URL=
# [R] Personal access token (mint at /app/settings/tokens)
# FONTO_PAT=
